# Byte-exactness guard for fixtures (Q1). The cross-os CI lane checks the
# repo out on Windows, and the GitHub windows-latest image sets
# core.autocrlf=true machine-wide — text-classified files would be
# CRLF-mangled at checkout, breaking golden byte comparisons. `-text`
# disables ALL end-of-line conversion under testdata/ so fixture bytes
# (G3 UTF-8 corpus inputs/outputs, Q4 golden vectors, Q7 tamper fixtures;
# layout owned by Q2) survive checkout unchanged on every OS.
testdata/** -text

# Production trust anchors compiled into antseal-core (D57 §7 / A6). Same
# byte-exactness hazard as testdata/, different tree: the rule above matches
# nothing under crates/, and a CRLF-mangled DER is an unparseable root — so
# without this line the pinned TSA root store silently stops working on a
# Windows checkout. Asserted from the crate itself by
# `anchor::roots::tests::the_gitattributes_binary_rule_covers_this_directory`,
# because the cross-os lane can only observe the damage on a Windows runner.
crates/antseal-core/src/anchor/roots/*.der -text
